      "_evidence": "BB group. In light of correlation findings, the RSES, the MPS socially prescribed subscale, the SPS, and the ORTO-15 were included in the second step of the two-steps hierarchical multiple regression. The overall model explained 49.1% of the variance in the MDDI total score. The DASS-21 total score was entered in the first step and significantly predicted the MDDI total score, F(1.40) = 6.62, p = 0.01, explaining 14% of the variation in the MDDI total score. The inclusion of the other variables in the second step explained an additional 41% of variation in the MDDI total score (F change = 8.27; p < 0.001). Results showed that, after controlling for the DASS-21 total score, the SPS and the ORTO-15 were significant predictors (β = 0.51 t = 3.95, p < 0.001 and β = −0.24 t = −2.12, p = 0.04, respectively), whereas the RSES (p = 0.06) and the MPS socially prescribed (p = 0.92) subscales were not.",
